1
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:37,110
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:41,110
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:45,110
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:50,110
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:53,110
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:56,110
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:59,110
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:02,110
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:05,110
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:05,110 --> 00:03:08,110
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:12,110
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:16,110
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:22,110
Separated from the rest of his crew,

14
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:26,110
Luffy has finally arrived at Marineford to rescue his brother Ace.

15
00:03:26,110 --> 00:03:30,110
Fighting alongside Whitebeard and his associates,

16
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:33,110
he continues to push toward the scaffold.

17
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:36,110
As the all-out battle continues between the Navy's elite

18
00:03:36,110 --> 00:03:38,110
and the strongest pirates in the world,

19
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:42,110
Luffy puts his life on the line, vowing death before defeat.

20
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:44,110
Concerned about the future?

21
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:47,110
I'll be more than happy to show it to you now.

22
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:48,110
Let's end this.

23
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:49,110
Execute him!

24
00:03:49,110 --> 00:03:54,110
I'm too slow!

25
00:03:54,110 --> 00:03:56,110
Don't make me laugh!

26
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:59,110
You think I can't stop those ruts from doing it?

27
00:03:59,110 --> 00:04:01,110
Don't use ruts from doing it!

28
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:20,110
Don't you dare!

29
00:04:29,110 --> 00:04:33,110
Don't use ruts from doing war.

30
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,110
Did you just do what I think you did?

31
00:04:39,110 --> 00:04:42,110
It's the conqueror's... spirit!

32
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:45,110
Well, damn. This is a mess.

33
00:04:45,110 --> 00:04:47,110
There's a surprise for you.

34
00:04:51,110 --> 00:04:53,110
Why that little brat?

35
00:04:53,110 --> 00:05:00,110
The scaffold at last! The way to Ace has opened!

36
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:13,110
We're good! Ace is still alive, guys!

37
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:18,110
Hey, pull it together, pal. That power, it came from Ace's brother, huh?

38
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:19,110
What the...?

39
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:21,110
I almost passed out back there.

40
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:31,110
That was the Conqueror's spirit, like Pops and Shanks use.

41
00:05:31,110 --> 00:05:34,110
Damn, that kid is full of surprises, huh?

42
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:38,110
I don't think he realizes what he just did.

43
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:42,110
I tell you, boys, we got some scary stuff right here.

44
00:05:42,110 --> 00:05:53,110
He didn't learn that power. He was born with it.

45
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:55,110
Just like Pops.

46
00:05:55,110 --> 00:06:03,110
If your will is weak, stand back. He's not just another rookie. Conqueror's spirit, huh?

47
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:08,110
We can't forget he's the son of Dragon. That's what we get for underestimating him.

48
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:09,110
What next, Vice Admiral?

49
00:06:09,110 --> 00:06:13,110
My energy hormones didn't do that. What hat did you pull those powers out of?

50
00:06:13,110 --> 00:06:15,110
Power? What do you mean?

51
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:16,110
We'll discuss it later.

52
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:20,110
He's not aware of it. That means we can't count on him using it again.

53
00:06:20,110 --> 00:06:23,110
Either way, it's no wonder the people are so drawn to him.

54
00:06:23,110 --> 00:06:26,110
The apple doesn't fall far from the tree, does it?

55
00:06:26,110 --> 00:06:27,110
Dragon.

56
00:06:27,110 --> 00:06:35,110
Do not let that boy escape this battlefield. If he does, he'll turn into a dire threat to us.

57
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:38,110
Dead or alive, you take him down!

58
00:06:38,110 --> 00:06:40,110
No!

59
00:06:57,110 --> 00:07:10,110
Scared to death of a mere boy and an old man? You were so cocky before, but where's your fire now?

60
00:07:10,110 --> 00:07:12,110
I thought you wanted to kill me!

61
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:26,110
Focus on Whitebeard first! He may be a monster, but he's injured! Take him down, then go for the kid!

62
00:07:26,110 --> 00:07:29,110
Hmm. Just try it.

63
00:07:31,110 --> 00:07:33,110
Don't let a single marine lay a hand on him!

64
00:07:36,110 --> 00:07:38,110
Don't be intimidated! Go!

65
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:43,110
They're aiming for Whitebeard! Move those buns while you still can!

66
00:07:43,110 --> 00:07:45,110
After Straw Hat! Hurry!

67
00:07:45,110 --> 00:07:46,110
Hurry!

68
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:47,110
Sir!

69
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:48,110
Uh...

70
00:07:48,110 --> 00:07:49,110
Um...

71
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:50,110
Huh?

72
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:51,110
Ah!

73
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:53,110
Ah!

74
00:07:54,110 --> 00:07:55,110
Ah!

75
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:56,110
Ah!

76
00:07:56,110 --> 00:07:58,110
Ah!

77
00:07:58,110 --> 00:07:59,110
Ah!

78
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:00,110
Ah!

79
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:02,110
Ah!

80
00:08:02,110 --> 00:08:03,110
Ah!

81
00:08:03,110 --> 00:08:04,110
Ah!

82
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:16,350
We finally make headway and the bastards start pulling it together.

83
00:08:17,570 --> 00:08:19,130
Thinks he can push through.

84
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:21,550
He'll be pushing up daisies first.

85
00:08:22,910 --> 00:08:23,910
Damn it all.

86
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:27,010
Crap. Come on.

87
00:08:27,610 --> 00:08:28,630
I can't help them.

88
00:08:28,830 --> 00:08:30,630
As long as I've got these things on.

89
00:08:30,850 --> 00:08:34,030
Hey, Pops. We got your back, so don't overdo it.

90
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:37,390
Stop and listen to me.

91
00:08:38,470 --> 00:08:39,450
What's wrong?

92
00:08:40,610 --> 00:08:42,130
There's a new plan.

93
00:08:42,510 --> 00:08:45,110
I'm either gonna live or I'm gonna die.

94
00:08:45,590 --> 00:08:49,230
So back up Straw Hat with everything you've got.

95
00:08:58,110 --> 00:08:59,870
Ace's brother? Why?

96
00:09:01,070 --> 00:09:02,290
What the hell?

97
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:05,510
Stop your gawking and take out Straw Hat already.

98
00:09:08,510 --> 00:09:11,210
They're coming straight at you. Watch out!

99
00:09:11,210 --> 00:09:16,750
I know you.

100
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:20,130
You're Doma, the Bohemian Knight, correct?

101
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:23,910
Vice Admiral Momonga. Pleasure to meet you.

102
00:09:23,910 --> 00:09:33,510
We're the Kelvin brothers. It sucks to be you.

103
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:35,010
You gotta fight us!

104
00:09:36,590 --> 00:09:38,050
Thunder Lord McGuy.

105
00:09:38,130 --> 00:09:41,750
Pardon me, Vice Admiral, but I require a moment of your time if you would.

106
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:45,210
We've got some friends.

107
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:48,750
If Whitebeard says to lend you a hand, then we're on it in a flash.

108
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:50,350
Ace is right there, Straw Hat.

109
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:52,650
No way they're gonna stop all of us.

110
00:09:52,710 --> 00:09:53,210
Yeah!

111
00:09:56,710 --> 00:09:58,830
Whitebeard's allies are backing up Straw Hat.

112
00:09:58,830 --> 00:10:00,250
This does not look good.

113
00:10:05,050 --> 00:10:06,290
Who are you guys?

114
00:10:06,630 --> 00:10:08,250
Never mind that. Keep running.

115
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:11,010
The Navy forces are focused on Pops right now.

116
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:14,910
So this might be your only chance to slip past the Admirals and move in.

117
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:18,170
We're sniping them all at once, so wait for your opening!

118
00:10:20,330 --> 00:10:23,150
Hey, not bad. I think they like you.

119
00:10:23,450 --> 00:10:26,510
The greatest pirate in the world gave his seal of approval.

120
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:27,030
Huh?

121
00:10:28,070 --> 00:10:28,710
Yee-haw!

122
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:33,850
Ace may be your brother, but he's Whitebeard's son, you know, and trusts you with his life.

123
00:10:34,070 --> 00:10:38,770
So why don't you stop trying to be coy and rise to the occasion, you cocky little snot?

124
00:10:39,090 --> 00:10:42,930
I don't care what that old man wants, and I don't care what he thinks either!

125
00:10:42,930 --> 00:10:45,650
I only came here to do one thing!

126
00:10:47,150 --> 00:10:49,510
I don't need anyone's approval for that!

127
00:10:50,410 --> 00:10:52,310
The pirates are gaining headway on us!

128
00:10:52,430 --> 00:10:55,550
They're about to break through! We need backup in a hurry!

129
00:10:55,630 --> 00:10:58,270
With all due respect, maybe we should change plans!

130
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:02,210
Not yet. If we have a chance to defeat Whitebeard, then we must take it!

131
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:03,730
Everyone move in now!

132
00:11:04,170 --> 00:11:07,290
If he falls, then it's only a matter of time for the rest of them!

133
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:11,170
One or one hundred doesn't matter.

134
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:14,410
You can stand in line, or you can all die at once!

135
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:31,370
He's still up! What's it going to take?

136
00:11:31,370 --> 00:11:38,910
We think alike, brat. As long as Ace goes home, nothing else matters.

137
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:43,030
Show me the will of Dee. Show me the future.

138
00:11:43,690 --> 00:11:48,410
Even if my days are numbered, I can see tomorrow blazing through this battlefield.

139
00:11:49,590 --> 00:11:52,910
Uh, Hawkeye! This could get nasty!

140
00:11:52,910 --> 00:12:04,870
It's the president's order. For now, we're still allies. Go!

141
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:09,990
Mr. One, I believe.

142
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:18,630
Look out!

143
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:29,950
Crocodile Two?

144
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:34,190
Stop sleeping on the job, Mr. One.

145
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:38,510
Uh, I thought it was like old times, but maybe prison made me soft.

146
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:43,490
You are needed here, Straw Hat. Get moving, before I change my mind.

147
00:12:47,830 --> 00:12:51,070
This won't end well. Are you certain?

148
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:55,050
I'm not in the mood to put up with your crap or anyone else's.

149
00:12:55,270 --> 00:12:57,490
If you want to fight, then shut up and do it.

150
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,110
Luffy! I'm here!

151
00:13:03,830 --> 00:13:05,970
I'll do everything in my power to aid you.

152
00:13:08,470 --> 00:13:11,150
Target is Monkey D. Luffy. Open fire.

153
00:13:11,150 --> 00:13:24,330
Boa Hancock. In sight. Aborting the attack.

154
00:13:24,650 --> 00:13:25,570
That's enough!

155
00:13:30,190 --> 00:13:32,010
Are you out of your damn mind?

156
00:13:32,330 --> 00:13:35,810
This isn't the first time you've gotten in the way, but it will be the last.

157
00:13:35,990 --> 00:13:38,090
What are you trying to accomplish here, anyway?

158
00:13:38,470 --> 00:13:40,550
You're going to lose your warlord status.

159
00:13:40,550 --> 00:13:44,470
You foolish, misshapen man-child.

160
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:46,870
Your ignorance is an affront to my beauty.

161
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:48,450
My what now?

162
00:13:48,590 --> 00:13:50,950
I shall set a pearl of wisdom before you.

163
00:13:51,730 --> 00:13:54,590
Love is always a hurricane, you little pig!

164
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:56,890
You're insane, aren't you?

165
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:24,210
You better run, Straw Hat.

166
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:28,010
So what's going on, Captain?

167
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:30,210
You don't seem too happy right now.

168
00:14:30,210 --> 00:14:32,530
I'm not. It doesn't look good out there.

169
00:14:32,530 --> 00:14:34,450
All of you saw it, right?

170
00:14:34,530 --> 00:14:36,450
How incredible I was on my broadcast.

171
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:38,370
The whole world should be watching me.

172
00:14:38,370 --> 00:14:39,830
But nobody cares!

173
00:14:39,830 --> 00:14:43,910
They're too busy gawking at that chump running to the scaffold to face their eyes on whatever

174
00:14:43,910 --> 00:14:45,770
awesome thing I happen to be doing.

175
00:14:45,770 --> 00:14:49,690
Now answer me this, who should be the star of this pirate show?

176
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:51,610
That would be you, of course.

177
00:14:51,610 --> 00:14:53,610
Damn straight it should be me.

178
00:14:53,610 --> 00:14:57,990
Now I've got to do something flashy in a flash so people stop watching Straw Hat's shenanigans

179
00:14:57,990 --> 00:14:59,290
and pay attention to mine.

180
00:14:59,290 --> 00:15:01,290
Hey, fork over that snail, pal.

181
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:02,810
Oh yeah, about that.

182
00:15:02,810 --> 00:15:03,610
The snail.

183
00:15:03,610 --> 00:15:06,030
It's kind of frozen solid right now.

184
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:06,990
What a pain!

185
00:15:06,990 --> 00:15:08,610
Just defrost the damn thing.

186
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:12,570
Give it a quick dip in that magma water or whatever and the ice should melt right off.

187
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:15,690
It melted, all right.

188
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:16,490
Nice!

189
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:17,490
Let me see.

190
00:15:17,490 --> 00:15:19,990
Good as new.

191
00:15:19,990 --> 00:15:20,990
Here.

192
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:22,990
It's all gross!

193
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:23,990
What did you do?

194
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:26,990
Oh yeah, salt water and snails don't get along, do they?

195
00:15:26,990 --> 00:15:30,990
After we went to all that trouble to steal it from the Navy, too.

196
00:15:30,990 --> 00:15:34,990
Well, it's not going to win any beauty contests, but the thing might still work.

197
00:15:34,990 --> 00:15:36,990
I'll just try to sweet-talk it a bit.

198
00:15:36,990 --> 00:15:40,990
Hey, little buddy, think you could open those peepers for me?

199
00:15:42,570 --> 00:15:45,450
We're going to be best buddies, okay?

200
00:15:45,450 --> 00:15:48,950
What?

201
00:15:48,950 --> 00:15:54,150
I was nice!

202
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:56,990
It's because of your scary faces, you bunch of goons.

203
00:15:56,990 --> 00:15:58,810
Sorry, I was born this way.

204
00:15:58,810 --> 00:16:00,990
I guess good looks don't run in my family.

205
00:16:00,990 --> 00:16:01,990
Damn it.

206
00:16:01,990 --> 00:16:05,450
Once Straw Hat makes it to that scaffold, nobody's going to care about anything else.

207
00:16:05,450 --> 00:16:07,450
I've got to do something distracting.

208
00:16:07,450 --> 00:16:14,450
Fire!

209
00:16:14,450 --> 00:16:20,370
Make a path to the scaffold!

210
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:25,330
We only need one moment to break through!

211
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:30,450
Getting desperate, are they?

212
00:16:30,450 --> 00:16:35,370
They're going to danger, noo, noo, noo!

213
00:16:58,110 --> 00:16:58,970
That's enough.

214
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:12,450
Fishman Karate!

215
00:17:13,450 --> 00:17:15,450
Arabesque Brickfish!

216
00:17:21,450 --> 00:17:24,450
Jinbei, I can handle this, dammit.

217
00:17:24,450 --> 00:17:29,450
I said to leave me and help Straw Hat get to the scaffold, didn't I?

218
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:32,450
Sorry friend, but I'm not one of your pirates.

219
00:17:32,450 --> 00:17:35,450
That means I don't have to listen to a word you say.

220
00:17:36,450 --> 00:17:38,450
Have it your way then.

221
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:07,450
They did it! They cleared a path!

222
00:18:08,450 --> 00:18:12,450
Everyone else has already done their part, now you do yours!

223
00:18:12,450 --> 00:18:14,450
Keep on running and don't look back!

224
00:18:14,450 --> 00:18:20,450
For better or worse, it's our turn now.

225
00:18:21,450 --> 00:18:24,450
Look, I'm sorry to make you do this when I know you're still recovering,

226
00:18:24,450 --> 00:18:27,450
but we need your skills in particular.

227
00:18:28,450 --> 00:18:30,450
No apologies necessary, I assure you.

228
00:18:31,450 --> 00:18:33,450
I shall give it my best.

229
00:18:33,450 --> 00:18:42,450
I'll try!

230
00:18:42,450 --> 00:18:43,450
I'll try!

231
00:18:43,450 --> 00:18:44,450
See you later!

232
00:18:44,450 --> 00:18:48,450
I'll find the world.

233
00:18:48,450 --> 00:18:53,450
How is that?!

234
00:18:53,450 --> 00:18:58,450
spikes fishing

235
00:18:58,450 --> 00:19:00,450
두들

236
00:19:01,450 --> 00:19:04,450
liegt

237
00:19:04,450 --> 00:19:18,030
They made a bridge!

238
00:19:18,670 --> 00:19:21,270
It's Sinasuma of the Revolutionary Army!

239
00:19:21,510 --> 00:19:23,990
Is that handy or what? Thanks!

240
00:19:24,510 --> 00:19:27,450
Straw Hutt's headed straight for the scaffold! Stop him!

241
00:19:27,770 --> 00:19:29,510
Sorry, too busy to do it myself!

242
00:19:29,970 --> 00:19:31,910
What are you doing? Block his path!

243
00:19:31,910 --> 00:19:35,910
We can't, sir! See? These pirates are blocking us! We can't get past!

244
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:39,910
Fools! Use your guns! Cannoneers open fire!

245
00:19:54,910 --> 00:19:56,910
Damn, it's them!

246
00:19:57,910 --> 00:20:00,910
The Whitebeard Pirates Team of Commanders!

247
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:07,910
Pop said to watch your back! So keep running! We got this!

248
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:13,910
Everyone push! We're breaking through!

249
00:20:13,910 --> 00:20:14,910
You!

250
00:20:29,910 --> 00:20:30,910
Here he comes, man!

251
00:20:30,910 --> 00:20:31,910
Come, come!

252
00:20:31,910 --> 00:20:32,910
Come, come!

253
00:20:34,910 --> 00:20:36,910
Battleaxe!

254
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:44,910
Take it straight to the top!

255
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,910
You got it! Thanks!

256
00:20:47,910 --> 00:20:49,910
He's getting away!

257
00:20:50,910 --> 00:20:52,910
Death wing!

258
00:20:55,910 --> 00:20:57,910
If you really want to rumble, then step right up!

259
